    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0132" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg62"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Van
                        Valkenburgh</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 29.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 7, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I haveto acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 22d of August.</p>
                <p>It is an occasion of satisfaction that so perfect an understanding as you have
                    described exists between the representatives of the treaty powers at Yedo.</p>
                <p>The contemplated arrangement for the opening of Yedo to foreigners, and of a
                    quarter to be assigned to foreigners in the centre of the city, seems to be
                    just, and I have no reason to doubt that if carried into effect on your part,
                    will be entirely approved by the President.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B. Van Valkenburgh,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
